{"kind":"report","text":"Planner read of the journey views design successor at 911d8c16951ade750eb1c49fb17ef98763482a9a. The read is bounded to P1 and R1 of 360efc4e. Result: both are resolved, and this exact candidate meets the planner read that a9a3585c requires.\n\nCoverage: I read the note's diff from fce231e0 in full, including the new section \"Planner catch-up correction\" and its table of scoped ranges. I viewed needs-you light 1536 (the changes element), needs-partial dark 390 (the changes element) and change-review light 1536. I read the checker's approval 9f014ba8 for the rest of the packet.\n\nP1, resolved. Needs you now lists every loaded entry under \"Since your last review\", grouped by scope. Each entry shows its number, the actor's kind and controller, what happened in plain words, and a link to the subject at that exact entry. Each group names its previous point and how far it was listed. Mark reviewed comes after the list and records only the ranges listed, and its text says so. In the partial state the unread scope is named, its saved point stays at 8, Load more is offered and Mark reviewed is disabled. On the phone the list comes before the only enabled Mark reviewed control. This meets plan 032 J5: \"the view shows everything that changed since mark reviewed\".\n\nR1, resolved. The checker marker is an outlined diamond and no longer looks like a form control.\n\nA note for the J5 implementation, not a finding on this design: in the partial state, Mark reviewed could later cover the fully loaded scopes on their own. Disabling it until every scope is read is the simpler rule for now. Keep it unless the exit test shows that it costs people time.\n\nThis is not an approval of runtime, host conformance or deployment. The views slices (MVP S2, S4 and S6, J2 and J5) may now take this design as their base once it lands.","body":{"findings":"none; P1 and R1 resolved","head":"911d8c16951ade750eb1c49fb17ef98763482a9a","planner_read":"met","request":"git:s